The interaction is LINEAR in SES: adding Black:SES^2 on top of Black:SES gives chi2=0.01, p=0.91. But the fully model-free Black x quintile-dummy version is only suggestive (p=0.12 unadjusted, p=0.07 adjusted) - the 4-df test loses power to the sparse cells, so the linear-interaction p~0.015 is the best-powered statement, not a robustness-free one.

